Chapter: RocPolyNopayloadVariant
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_issue_tests.zig, "issue 9502:
 static dispatch on no-payload variant of polymorphic nominal evaluates":

     Foo(a) := [Bar(a), Baz].{ inspect = |_foo| "ok" }
     main = Foo.inspect(Baz)                                      "ok"

 The no-payload constructor of a polymorphic sum is passed where nothing
 constrains the parameter. The port adds a second line that DOES constrain
 it, through `Bar 1`, so the two uses sit side by side.

Section: Types

  Foo (a) =
   | Bar (a)
   | Baz

Section: Functions

  inspect-foo : Foo a -> Text
  inspect-foo (ignored) = "ok"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (inspect-foo Baz)
   print-line-uni (inspect-foo (Bar 1))
  end
